.TH DIFFVIM 1 "2026-08-11" "diffvim 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffvim \- animate a code diff in vim as if a human were typing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.RI <oldfile>
.RI <newfile>

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-multi
.RI <old1:new1>
.RI <old2:new2>
\&...

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-replay
.RI <file>
.RB [ \-\-from
.IR REV ]
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR REV ]

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-git-rev
.IR REV..REV
.RI <file>
[<file> ...]

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-diff
.IR FILE
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]

.br
.B diffvim
.B \-\-version
.br
.B diffvim
.B \-\-help

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffvim
opens the old version of a file in vim and animates the transformation into
the new version character by character. The cursor glides between change
locations with smooth ease-in-out acceleration, and only the actually-changed
characters are deleted and re-typed \(em surrounding text is never touched.

After the animation completes (or the user stops it), the buffer is a normal
vim buffer and can be edited, saved, or quit normally.

Three implementations are available:
.TP
.B diffvim
Bash launcher + embedded Vimscript engine. Uses vim's native
.BR timer_start ()
for async animation. No external dependencies beyond vim 8+. Best for
everyday use.
.TP
.B diffvim-tmux
Bash orchestrator + vim in a tmux pane. Bash sends Ex commands to vim via
.BR tmux\ send-keys .
Requires bash 4+, tmux 3+, vim 8+, diff, sed, awk.
.TP
.B diffvim.pl
Perl orchestrator + vim in a tmux pane. Same architecture as diffvim-tmux
but with pluggable diff parser modules. Requires Perl 5.10+, tmux 3+, vim 8+.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS Core Options

.TP
.BR \-\-speed\  N
Speed multiplier.
.B 0.5
= half speed,
.B 2
= double speed,
.B 5
= 5x speed.
All timing delays are divided by this value.
Also settable via
.B DIFFVIM_SPEED
environment variable.

.TP
.BI \-\-output\  FILE
After the animation completes, write the buffer to
.I FILE
and quit vim. Also works with
.B q
(quit) \(em the buffer is written before stopping.

.TP
.BR \-\-scroll\  zz | zt | zb | none
Scroll the cursor to the specified position during animation:
.RS
.TP 4
.B zz
Center cursor on screen
.TP 4
.B zt
Cursor at top of screen
.TP 4
.B zb
Cursor at bottom of screen
.TP 4
.B none
Don't force scroll (default)
.RE

.TP
.B \-\-multi
Treat arguments as
.I old:new
pairs for multi-file animation. After finishing one file, the animation
transitions to the next.

.TP
.BI \-\-context\  N
Fold unchanged regions longer than 2*N lines, keeping N lines of context
around each hunk. Default: 0 (no folding).

.SS Diff Options

.TP
.BR \-\-parser\  perl | diff2html
(diffvim.pl only) Diff parser to use.
.B perl
uses a pure-Perl LCS algorithm (default, no deps).
.B diff2html
shells out to the
.B diff2html
CLI with
.B \-f json
for line-level parsing.

.TP
.B \-\-word-diff
Use word-level diff instead of char-level. Groups changes by word
(non-space sequences), producing more natural typing patterns.

.TP
.BR \-\-algorithm\  lcs | myers | patience
Line-level diff algorithm.
.B lcs
(default) uses classic LCS dynamic programming.
.B myers
uses O(ND) Myers algorithm (falls back to LCS for correctness).
.B patience
anchors on unique common lines for more human-readable diffs.

.TP
.BI \-\-max-hunk-chars\  N
If a hunk has more than N changed characters, skip the char-by-char
animation and apply the entire hunk instantly.

.TP
.BI \-\-max-word-chars\  N
If a contiguous sequence of modified (non-space) characters is LONGER
than N, apply the whole sequence in one shot with a pause, so the user
can read the change. Sequences <= N are animated character by character.

.TP
.BI \-\-word-pause-ms\  N
Pause in milliseconds after an instant word is applied (only relevant
with
.BR \-\-max-word-chars ).
Default: 150.

.TP
.BI \-\-max-line-len\  N
Warn if any line exceeds N characters (char-level diff may be slow).
Default: 10000.

.TP
.B \-\-semantic-cleanup
Post-process char ops to merge adjacent insert/delete pairs that cancel
out, reducing unnecessary typing.

.TP
.B \-\-indent-aware
Normalize indentation before line-level diff, so lines that differ only
in indentation are treated as "keep" at the line level.

.SS Git Options

.TP
.B \-\-replay
Animate git history for the given file(s). For each commit in the range,
extracts the old version and animates the transformation to the next commit.

.TP
.BI \-\-from\  REV
Git revision to start replay from. Default:
.BR HEAD~5 .

.TP
.BI \-\-to\  REV
Git revision to end replay at. Default:
.BR HEAD .

.TP
.BI \-\-git-rev\  REV..REV
Animate a git commit range using
.I REV..REV
syntax. Shorthand for
.B \-\-replay \-\-from REV1 \-\-to REV2.

.TP
.B \-\-git-blame
Show git blame information for each changed line.

.SS Animation Options

.TP
.B \-\-step-mode
Space advances one char op at a time instead of toggling pause/resume,
for detailed inspection.

.TP
.B \-\-adaptive-timing
Automatically slow down for complex hunks (many char ops close together)
and speed up for simple ones.

.TP
.B \-\-sign-column
Show
.B +/-
signs in vim's sign column to indicate deleted/added lines.

.TP
.B \-\-highlight-hunk
Visually highlight the hunk region before animating it. The highlight
is shown for
.B \-\-highlight-duration-ms
milliseconds, then cleared.

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-color\  COLOR
Vim highlight group for hunk highlighting. Default:
.BR DiffChange .
Also:
.BR DiffAdd ,
.BR DiffDelete ,
.BR Search ,
.BR Visual ,
.BR IncSearch .

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-duration-ms\  N
Highlight duration in milliseconds. Default: 1000.

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-min-chars\  N
Minimum changed chars to trigger hunk highlighting. Default: 10.
Hunks with fewer changed chars are animated without highlighting.

.TP
.B \-\-fold-unchanged
Fold unchanged regions between hunks so the user only sees the changes.
Press
.B f
during animation to toggle folding on/off.

.TP
.BR \-\-theme\  dark | light | high-contrast
Color scheme for animation highlights:
.RS
.TP 4
.B dark
Set background=dark
.TP 4
.B light
Set background=light
.TP 4
.B high-contrast
Vivid green/red/yellow diff highlights
.RE

.SS Utility Options

.TP
.B \-\-no-tmux
(diffvim.pl only) Run vim directly in the terminal (no tmux wrapper).
Simpler single-shot use, but no FIFO-based user input.

.TP
.B \-\-remote
(diffvim.pl only) Use
.B vim \-\-remote-send
with
.B \-\-servername
instead of tmux send-keys. Eliminates tmux race conditions.

.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Compute and print the diff ops without launching vim. Useful for
debugging parser issues.

.TP
.B \-\-diff\  FILE
Accept a unified diff/patch file as input instead of requiring two files.
Use
.B \-
for stdin. Enables:
.B git diff | diffvim \-\-diff \-

.TP
.B \-\-parser-compare
(diffvim.pl only) Run both parsers and report any differences in the
computed hunks. Exit code 0 if all match, 1 if any mismatch.

.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose logging of all Ex commands sent, with timestamps, to
.BR /tmp/diffvim-debug.log .
Useful for debugging race conditions and timing issues.

.TP
.BR \-\-version ,\  \-V
Print version, parser info, and dependency versions (vim, tmux, perl,
diff2html).

.TP
.BR \-\-help ,\  \-h
Show help message and exit.

.SH CONTROLS
During animation, the following keys are active in vim normal mode:

.SS Basic Controls
.TP
.B <Space>
Pause / resume the animation. In
.B \-\-step-mode ,
advances one char op instead.
.TP
.B n
Skip current hunk: apply all remaining character operations instantly
and move to the next hunk.
.TP
.B b
Back to previous hunk: revert the buffer to the state before the
current hunk started and replay it from the beginning.
.TP
.B q
Stop the animation. The buffer is left in its current state for normal
editing.

.SS Speed Controls
.TP
.B +
Speed up: multiply the current speed by 1.5.
.TP
.B \-
Slow down: divide the current speed by 1.5.
.TP
.B =
Reset speed to 1.0x.

.SS Granular Navigation
.TP
.B B
(Shift-B) Go back one char op.
.TP
.B N
(Shift-N) Skip to next file (multi-file mode).
.TP
.B Ctrl-B
Go back to the beginning.
.TP
.B Ctrl-N
Skip to the end.

.SS Undo/Redo
.TP
.B u
Undo last hunk (revert to previous snapshot).
.TP
.B Ctrl-r
Redo hunk.

.SS Display
.TP
.B ?
Toggle full-screen help overlay.
.TP
.B f
Toggle fold on/off (with
.BR \-\-fold-unchanged ).

.SS Progress
A progress message is shown in the vim status line:
.RS
.PP
.nf
diffvim: hunk 3/7 (42%) | speed 2.3x | PAUSED
.fi
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
All timing values can be set via environment variables. Command-line
options override environment variables, which override built-in defaults.

.TP
.B DIFFVIM_TICK_MS
Animation frame interval in milliseconds (default: 16, ~60fps).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_TYPE_DELAY_MS
Delay between typed characters in milliseconds (default: 35).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_DELETE_DELAY_MS
Delay between deleted characters in milliseconds (default: 25).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MIN_MS
Minimum cursor glide duration in milliseconds (default: 200).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MAX_MS
Maximum cursor glide duration in milliseconds (default: 1400).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MS_PER_UNIT
Milliseconds per unit of glide distance (default: 6). Lines are weighted
80x more than columns.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HUNK_PAUSE_MS
Pause between hunks in milliseconds (default: 180).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_WORD_PAUSE_MS
Pause after instant word in milliseconds (default: 150).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_SPEED
Speed multiplier (default: 1.0). Same as
.BR \-\-speed .
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MAX_LINE_LEN
Warn threshold for long lines (default: 10000).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_COLOR
Highlight group for
.B \-\-highlight-hunk
(default: DiffChange).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_DURATION_MS
Highlight duration in ms (default: 1000).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_MIN_CHARS
Min changed chars to trigger highlight (default: 10).

.SH EXAMPLES

.SS Basic Usage
.PP
.nf
diffvim old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Speed Control
.PP
.nf
# Half speed for a presentation
diffvim \-\-speed 0.5 old.py new.py

# 3x speed for quick review
diffvim \-\-speed 3 old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Output
.PP
.nf
# Write result to file and quit
diffvim \-\-output result.py old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Display Options
.PP
.nf
# Center cursor, highlight hunks, fold unchanged regions
diffvim \-\-scroll zz \-\-highlight-hunk \-\-fold-unchanged old.py new.py

# High-contrast theme
diffvim \-\-theme high-contrast old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Diff Algorithms
.PP
.nf
# Use patience diff for more human-readable hunks
diffvim \-\-algorithm patience old.py new.py

# Word-level diff
diffvim \-\-word-diff old.py new.py

# Semantic cleanup
diffvim \-\-semantic-cleanup old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Word Batching
.PP
.nf
# Sequences > 5 chars are applied in one shot with a pause
diffvim \-\-max-word-chars 5 old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Multi-file Animation
.PP
.nf
diffvim \-\-multi old1.py:new1.py old2.py:new2.py
.fi

.SS Git Integration
.PP
.nf
# Replay last 5 commits of a file
diffvim \-\-replay src/main.py

# Specific commit range
diffvim \-\-replay src/main.py \-\-from v1.0 \-\-to HEAD

# Using \-\-git-rev syntax
diffvim \-\-git-rev HEAD~3..HEAD src/main.py

# Show git blame during animation
diffvim \-\-git-blame old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Unified Diff Input
.PP
.nf
# Animate from a patch file
diffvim \-\-diff my.patch

# From stdin
git diff | diffvim \-\-diff \-
.fi

.SS Debugging
.PP
.nf
# Dry run (print ops without launching vim)
diffvim \-\-dry-run old.py new.py

# Verbose logging
diffvim \-\-debug old.py new.py
cat /tmp/diffvim-debug.log

# Compare parsers
diffvim \-\-parser-compare old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Vim Plugin
.PP
.nf
# Inside an existing vim session:
:Diffvim old.py new.py
:Diffvim old.py new.py tabnew
.fi

